   3               / THIS HANDLER ALLOWS OUTPUT ON A LINEPRINTER WITHOUT
   4               /SACRIFICING THE OS/8 FILE OUTPUT CAPABILITY FOR THIS
   5               /PURPOSE.   THIS VERSION WILL NOT WORK WITH THE LATER
   6               /KL8E-STYLE INTERFACE SINCE IT TAKES ADVANTAGE OF THE
   7               /'6667' INSTRUCTION TO PREVENT INTERRUPTS.   THE ECHO
   8               /OPTION MAY BE SPECIFIED IN THE USUAL WAY TO CREATE A
   9               /COPY OF THE OUTPUT ON THE TERMINAL.  IT IS ALSO POS-
  10               /SIBLE TO MAKE THE LPT:  THE DEFAULT OUTPUT DEVICE SO
  11               /THAT ERROR MESSAGES, ECHOING FROM AN OS/8 FILE, ETC.
  12               /WILL  APPEAR ON THE  LINEPRINTER  RATHER THAN ON THE
  13               /TERMINAL.   THIS IS SPECIFIED BY THE 'O E'  ('OUTPUT
  14               /EVERYTHING'!)  COMMAND: 'O E LPT:'.   IF YOU SPECIFY
  15               /THE ECHO OPTION IN  -THIS-  COMMAND YOU WILL GET -3-
  16               /COPIES OF THE OUTPUT!  1) ORIGINAL TO THE OS/8 FILE;
  17               /2) A COPY ON THE LPT: AND 3) A COPY ON THE TERMINAL!
